        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c1e384ea-37a9-5542-9bf7-dcb00f36fe36",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Susanna Thompson, Rob Reiner, Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, James Woods, Stephen Amell, Willa Holland, David Ramsey, Colin Donnell, Katie Cassidy, Paul Blackthorne\n- Works: Little Giants, Ghosts of Mississippi, Random Hearts, Dragonfly, Once and Again, Arrow, Pilot\n- Roles: Karen Sammler, Moira Queen, Oliver Queen, Thea, John Diggle, Tommy Merlyn, Laurel Lance, Quentin Lance\n\nFacts:\n- Susanna Thompson was born on January 27, 1958, and she is an American actress.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Little Giants in 1994.\n- Ghosts of Mississippi is a 1996 American biographical courtroom drama film directed by Rob Reiner and starring Alec Baldwin, Whoopi Goldberg, and James Woods.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Ghosts of Mississippi in 1996.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Random Hearts in 1999.\n- From 1999 to 2002, Susanna Thompson played Karen Sammler on the ABC drama series Once and Again.\n- Susanna Thompson appeared in the film Dragonfly in 2002.\n- In the Arrow episode Pilot, Stephen Amell plays Oliver Queen, and Susanna Thompson plays his mother, Moira Queen.\n- In the Arrow episode Pilot, Willa Holland plays Thea, David Ramsey plays John Diggle, Colin Donnell plays Tommy Merlyn, Katie Cassidy plays Laurel Lance, and Paul Blackthorne plays Detective Quentin Lance.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
